# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://github.com/l0v3m0n3y/imgur"
      }
      description: "This API provides access to the functionalities of Imgur, allowing users to find, rate, and share memes and images from the platform. It enables easy integration with various applications, offering capabilities such as retrieving image metadata and managing user accounts."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Imgur API Server"
          url: "https://imgur.com"
        }
      ]
      title: "Imgur API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Find, rate, and share memes and images from the Imgur platform"
      homepage: "https://imgur.com"
      docs_url: "https://apidocs.imgur.com/"
      license_short: "Imgur API Terms of Service; requires registered application and Client ID"
      license_md: `- Use of the API is governed by Imgur's API Terms of Service and Developer Agreement.
- A registered application and Client ID are required; OAuth 2.0 is used for user-authenticated actions.
- Imgur-hosted images and user content remain the property of their respective owners; review Imgur's terms before redistributing content.`
      about_md: `[Imgur](https://imgur.com) is a community-driven image and meme sharing site. Its public HTTP API at \`https://api.imgur.com\` exposes the same image, gallery, and tag data that powers the Imgur website and mobile apps.

What you typically work with through this SDK:

- Image and media metadata served from Imgur's CDN
- Gallery / post discovery and tagging endpoints under \`/3/\` (for example \`GET /3/tags\`)
- Client configuration endpoints used by Imgur's own front-ends (for example \`GET /3/configuration/desktop\`)

Authentication is required: every request must include a registered application's Client ID via an \`Authorization: Client-ID <id>\` header, and user-scoped actions additionally require an OAuth 2.0 access token. Endpoints, quotas, and availability are defined by Imgur and have historically been unstable for third-party callers, so treat responses defensively.`
      entity_desc: {
        image: "An image or media item hosted on Imgur, including its CDN URL and associated metadata."
        post_meta: "Metadata about a gallery post or tag grouping, such as the tag listings returned by `GET /3/tags`."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
